  "assertions": [
    "A present MMS SMSKey containing NUL supplies named Receive evidence only when there are no extra selected-group children; absent/empty/NUL-free keys retain existing behavior.",
    "Complete containing scans verify unique selected ancestors and a closed MMS group with one Originator-Address and one key, optional known children at most once, correct vendor/flags and scalar widths.",
    "Owned quotes are 36+align4(payload length) bytes: two minimal vendor headers and the entire original key including padding, without address, sibling, subscriber or financial data.",
    "ErrField and the full vendor10415 path873/877/1210 remain. Build/Send and mixed extra children retain their original errors; ErrUnsupported is not added.",
    "Structural/nested address failures retain priority over the MMS callback, which retains priority over enclosing request conditions. No wire/group/root rule is reordered.",
    "Address and unrelated ancestor sibling payloads remain opaque to this trusted callback; the issuing decoder remains responsible for full validation.",
    "All32 optional-child combinations, exact and one-less limits, malformed instances, original padding, shared source counts and ownership are covered.",
    "TCP/TLS ordinary/emergency/default paths verify exact envelopes, non-delivery, held charges, follow-up and retirement; a short emergency reply budget closes without truncation.",
    "Local affected-target fuzz and complete hosted17-target receipts are separately counted.",
    "Pure Go, application-owned persistence, frozen rc.1 receipts, module requirements and immutable tags remain unchanged."
  ],
